<title>GERMANY: Holzmann sees breakeven in current year.</title>
<headline>Holzmann sees breakeven in current year.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction company Philipp Holzmann AG said on Friday it expected to break even in 1996, with a high level of orders in hand to ensure full capacity usage.</p>
<p>Holzmann also said in a statement that its group restructuring programme annnounced in June would proceed intensively in the months to come and would be completed by the end of 1997, as orginally planned.</p>
</text>
